<install>
  <update file="${package.root}/install/bundles" todir="${env.bundles}" />
  <copy dir="${package.root}/web" todir="${env.server.home}/nxserver" overwrite="true" />
  <!--
    Layer 0 configuration lives beside the application bundle rather than inside
    it, and the package ships only a SAMPLE of it: `bootstrap.example.json`.

    The destination must be inside the directory Tomcat actually serves. The
    `nuxeo` context declares docBase="../nxserver/nuxeo.war", so a request for
    `/nuxeo/agentic-ui-config/bootstrap.json` resolves to
    `nxserver/nuxeo.war/agentic-ui-config/bootstrap.json`. `nxserver/web` holds
    only `root.war` and is not a docBase; anything placed there is never served.

    The package must never install `bootstrap.json` itself, the file a customer
    creates and edits (NXSAT-317). An upgrade is an uninstall of the old version
    followed by an install of the new one. The uninstall deletes a package file
    only if its md5 still matches, so an edited file is left on disk, and a copy
    with overwrite="false" then fails on it. The install rolls back only its own
    commands, so the result is NO version installed and `/nuxeo/agentic-ui/`
    returning 404. Without overwrite="false", a copy would destroy the edit
    instead. A file nobody edits has neither problem, so the sample is
    package-owned and replaced with overwrite="true", and `bootstrap.json` is
    never touched by an install, an upgrade or an uninstall.

    The application treats a missing `bootstrap.json` as "use the compiled
    defaults", which the sample's values are, so a fresh install needs no copy.
    `review-guardrails.mjs` (checkInstallerOwnsNoCustomerFile) fails the build on
    any copy not declared overwrite="true" (Nuxeo's default is false), a packaged
    `bootstrap.json`, or any other file in the config directory, where it would
    replace a customer's same-named file, a logo for instance, on upgrade.
  -->
  <copy dir="${package.root}/config"
        todir="${env.server.home}/nxserver/nuxeo.war/agentic-ui-config"
        overwrite="true" />
</install>
